upstream:   corl-team/CORL
commit:     eeeeef2
generator:  bca/scripts/corl_verify/_corl_reference.py
scores:     docs/benchmarks/offline.md, the "## Last Scores" section ONLY
configs:    configs/offline/<algo>/<domain>/<dataset>.yaml

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. corl_reference_scores.csv is the provenance boundary for the whole
configuration chain: _published_config.py reads it to REFUSE a run that does not carry the
per-environment settings CORL's published number came from, and _corlorig_emit.py generates
the original-code config yamls from it. The generator records the upstream commit in its own
docstring and in the markdown it writes, but the CSV carried no revision of any kind, so a
regeneration against a different CORL revision would be invisible to every consumer.

The scores are CORL's LAST column, not Best. Those are different estimands and this project
has been burned by conflating them twice.
